==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{term|avec|lang=frm}}, {{term|avecques||with|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{term|avoc|lang=fro}}, {{term|avoec|lang=fro}}, {{term|avuec||with|lang=fro}}, from an assumed {{etyl|LL.|fr}} *{{term||aboc, *abhoc, *apud hŏque|lang=la}}<ref>"Brachet, ''An etymological dictionary of the French language'', avec.</ref><ref name=a>http://www.cnrtl.fr/etymologie/avec</ref>, a Frankish alteration consisting of {{etyl|la|fr}} {{term|apud||with, near, close to|lang=la}} + {{term/t|la|hōc||this}} + {{term|-que|lang=la}}.  First used as a replacement for {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|cum||with|lang=la}} in [[w:Merovingian|Merovingian]] and [[w:Carolingian|Carolingian]] (Frankish) documents. Gradually supplanted Old French {{term|od||with|lang=fro}}, itself from {{term|apud|lang=la}}.<ref name=a/>

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-avec.ogg|audio}}
